{"title":"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Expectation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Expectation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the average (mean) of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed by using each of the digits 1, 3, 5, 7, and 8 exactly once?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/02638524868f5a46b7c52bddd10e947bdb683bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }48000\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }49999.5\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }53332.8\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }55555\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }56432.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"579\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Expectation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Expectation)\">Solution 1 (Expectation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Expectation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The average of all valid numbers is simply the expected value of a randomly chosen valid number. In other words, it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/6/be61f8ac132713d9739411c3eca02e7d7b338fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E[\\text{ten thousands digit}]\\cdot 10^4+E[\\text{thousands digit}]\\cdot 10^3+\\cdots+E[\\text{ones digit}]\\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"586\" height=\"21\" />. However, every digit is equally likely to be chosen for every place, so we can simplify this to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6ccfee8022a62c7ccd599cb5cb3d62c028bcb77c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+3+5+7+8}{5}\\cdot(10^4+10^3+10^2+10^1+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"368\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73fbff3bf74ebc15b6114a55a907830578e2cd45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=4.8\\cdot11111 = \\boxed{(C) 53332.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"226\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first look at how many times each number will appear in each slot. If we fix a number in a slot, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/482b0fba62fc7502e8b9fb930374b8f096a3a940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4! = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> ways to arrange the other numbers, so each number appears in each spot <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times. Therefore, the sum of all such numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4cc4118e7a348814943a991add4c7e61f56eed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 \\times (1+3+5+7+8) \\times (11111) = 24 \\times 24 \\times 11111 = 6399936.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"512\" height=\"18\" /> Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a578519da397fe10b98efaa61cb1c65ca1b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5! = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" /> such numbers, we divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56ce8cb413a5b496bb5c21b4ba5ee264dc018d96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6399936 \\div 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb479e17808d2afd9d245e5046d0833da48a0b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }53332.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"108\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can first solve for the mean for the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/0/8302a520387ac35652ef30ab035f68c87b6911c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 3, 5, 7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> since each is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> away from each other. The mean of the numbers than can be solved using these digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb4cd19efe849fbfa0354edc068e3a43becff7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55555$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />. The total amount of numbers that can be formed using these digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb089404a0c876d2f88014e5dcd8c0241ede430f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5! =120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" />. The sum of these numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/933418a0cdf93fef85953ed72132f2804c94da92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55555(120) = 6666600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />. Now we can find out the total value that was gained by replacing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We can start how be calculating the gain when the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> was in the ones digit. Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/482b0fba62fc7502e8b9fb930374b8f096a3a940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4! = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> numbers with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the ones digit and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> was gain from each of them, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is the number gained. Then, we repeat this with the tens, hundreds, thousands, and ten thousands place, leading to a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/42634e28f052a41df511f6f0d9118e7664f77e38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24+240+2400+24000+240000=266664$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"349\" height=\"14\" /> as the total amount that was gained. Subtract this amount from the sum of the digits using the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> instead of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b25e809b1ca7436afab8b7ca1bf9b578abdfc97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6666600-266664=6399936$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"227\" height=\"13\" />. Finally, we divide this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> to get the average. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fce0d90bb2b9cdf5fafef41cbd90a97b16bff5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6399936}{120}= \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }53332.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ha3xtyz5bME\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ha3xtyz5bME</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B\">2005 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204547\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 249/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5526/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.763      1 -total\n 61.27%    7.820      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 37.63%    4.803      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3176:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017204547 and revision id 263391. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}